# Guide only

A guide step is the whole instruction. Do that step. Do not add a different action because the real control is hard to find.

1. Read the step text before acting. If the step does not name a canvas mode, do not switch Auto-Layout or Free-Form.
2. If the page is already in Auto-Layout, add the element with the plus on the path, then choose the element the step names.
3. A checker must compare the action with the step text before the click. If the action is not in the step, do not do it.
4. When a step fails, look at the page and the step again. Do not invent a second path that the guide never wrote.
5. Learn the miss. The same unguided action is not tried again on a later run.
